### implement-plugin-init (the active task)

Goal: Make plugin initialization self-contained so mypy can run from config alone — generating/refreshing manifest and stubs during plugin startup without external orchestration.

Details from plan.md:
- Tighten plugin config contract around `packages`, `roles`, `cache_dir`, `strict`
- Ensure init always regenerates manifest/stubs for package-driven configs (Phase 1A)
- Expose generated stub root to mypy via `options.mypy_path`
- Update automation contract so `just consumer-mypy` no longer depends on pre-generation
- Do not touch consumer source (`category_specs`); satisfy from plugin/config alone
- Phase 1A only: regenerate every run. Cache reuse waits until after always-regenerate is green.

